msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:219
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the number is prime, `false` otherwise. Set \"strict\" "
"boolean to true to force GRH-supported lower bound of 2*log(N)^2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:222
msgid "`bigInt(5).isPrime()` => `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:223
msgid "`bigInt(6).isPrime()` => `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:225
msgid "`isProbablePrime([iterations], [rng])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:227
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the number is very likely to be prime, `false` "
"otherwise. Supplying `iterations` is optional - it determines the number "
"of iterations of the test (default: `5`). The more iterations, the lower "
"chance of getting a false positive. This uses the [Miller Rabin "
"test](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miller%E2%80%93Rabin_primality_test)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:231
msgid "`bigInt(5).isProbablePrime()` => `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:232
msgid "`bigInt(49).isProbablePrime()` => `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:233
msgid "`bigInt(1729).isProbablePrime()` => `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:235
msgid ""
"Note that this function is not deterministic, since it relies on random "
"sampling of factors, so the result for some numbers is not always the "
"same - unless you pass a predictable random number generator as `rng`. "
"The behavior and requirements are the same as with `randBetween`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:237
msgid "`bigInt(1729).isProbablePrime(1, () => 0.1)` => `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:238
msgid "`bigInt(1729).isProbablePrime(1, () => 0.2)` => `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/big-integer_README.md:240
msgid ""
"If the number is composite then the Miller–Rabin primality test declares "
"the number probably prime with a probability at most `4` to the power "
"`−iterations`. If the number is prime, this function always returns "
"`true`."
msgstr ""

